+**Lot CI at freeze — `ameesh ci run <lot>` (#1343).** On a lot branch a push
+starts nothing (canon §3: review comes before CI); the lot CI (impacted +
+contract, `--mode lot`) is dispatched **once**, on the frozen head, when the
+required verdicts are acquired:
+
+```
+ameesh ci run <lot> [--avis 0|1|2] [--sha S] [--force] [--dry-run] [--json]
+ameesh ci cancel <lot> [--all] [--dry-run]
+```
+
+`ci run` refuses to dispatch unless the branch head is the last `frozen`
+milestone commit, `--avis N` verdicts `ok` were declared on that exact commit
+by distinct actors other than the assignee (0 for a lot léger, 1 for a
+sensible lot, 2 for SQL, security or prod), the workflow at that commit
+carries the trigger (an older branch is told to rebase on main), and no run
+was already seen on that commit: green or in flight returns without writing,
+red or cancelled needs `--force`. Before dispatching, the branch's open runs
+that do not carry the frozen commit are cancelled (canon §3); `ameesh ci
+cancel <lot>` does that alone, `--all` including the frozen run. The dispatch
+carries `mode`, `sha`, `base` (merge-base with the target) and `lot`; the
+`plan` job compares `sha` to `HEAD` and fails the required check, running no
+test, when the ref moved, and the `tests` aggregate refuses a green that ran
+no test (no version-only or documentation-only lane at freeze). An incident
+or a CI unblock dispatches in parallel of the review with `--exception
+incident|unblock --reason …`, marked in the run name and in a note on the
+lot; `--full --reason …` runs the whole suite (release, package, manual
+dispatch). `main`, `release/**`, the integration branch and release pull
+requests keep their automatic full suite.
+
 **Release pull requests keep the full suite (canon §3).** A pull request whose
 source or target is `release/**` or the integration branch runs the full suite
 under both drivers, like the push to those branches, whatever the map says: no
